  Any hostname not in the dev set falls back to [1mproduction[0m. That's deliberate: an unrecognized host is far more likely
  to be a real deployment than a dev box, and silently pointing a real user's login at a dev API is the worse failure.
  The tradeoff is that a typo'd dev hostname fails toward production instead of erroring loudly.

  [3mAssumption: [38;5;153mhttps://api.dev.example.com[39m is a placeholder — validate by replacing it with your real dev host before [0m
